        "text": "Chapter 1 I Mastering the Terminal Window\n29\nRemote Connections in Kali\nThere are two common ways to connect remotely to other operating systems.\nFor Windows, it is the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), and for Linux, it\u2019s the\nSecure Shell (SSH). In the next sections, I will explain how to use each protocol\nto connect remotely to an OS (Windows or Linux).\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Remote Desktop Protocol\n\u2022 Secure Shell\n\u2022 SSH with Credentials\n\u2022 Passwordless SSH\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
